## Activity

One timeline entry: `activityType` (note / call / email / meeting / status change, each with its own icon), `summary`, a markdown `body`, `occurredAt`, `author = linksTo(User)` and `about = linksTo(CardDef)`, so an activity can attach to any record — a deal, an opportunity, an account.

```ts
import { Activity } from '@cardstack/catalog/cards/crm/activity';

// Query Activity by type, then keep the ones about this record, newest first.
let timeline = (activities as Activity[])
  .filter((a) => a.about?.id === record.id)
  .sort((a, b) => +new Date(b.occurredAt) - +new Date(a.occurredAt));
```

The record holds no list of its activities. A timeline is a reverse-chronological query for `Activity` where `about` is that record, so logging an activity never has to write back to what it is about. The embedded format is the timeline row; to render a list of them, hand the results to the service desk's `Feed` (`@cardstack/catalog/cards/service-desk/components/feed`).

### Examples
Two entries on `Deal/acme-enterprise-renewal` (a call and a stage change), an email about `Opportunity/brightleaf-workspace` sent before it closed, a note on `Account/acme-industries`, and a meeting on `Account/brightleaf-studio` with no body.

**Non-goals:** reminders and scheduling, automatic capture from email or calendar sync, threaded comments.
